From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabian Sommer <fabiansommer@google.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Clamp ATR length in CmdPowerOn to received data

Ensure CmdPowerOn does not read past the actual number of bytes received
from ReadPort when extracting the ATR, preventing an uninitialized stack
read if a device reports a dwLength larger than the payload delivered.
---
 third_party/ccid/src/src/commands.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/ccid/src/src/commands.c b/third_party/ccid/src/src/commands.c
index 8642aafd..5790588d 100644
--- a/third_party/ccid/src/src/commands.c
+++ b/third_party/ccid/src/src/commands.c
@@ -282,6 +282,8 @@ again:
 	atr_len = dw2i(resp, 1);	/* ATR length */
 	if (atr_len > *nlength)
 		atr_len = *nlength;
+	if (atr_len > length - CCID_RESPONSE_HEADER_SIZE)
+		atr_len = length - CCID_RESPONSE_HEADER_SIZE;
 
 	*nlength = atr_len;
 
-- 
2.46.0
